  <data name="Set_DownloadsRiskTitle" xml:space="preserve"><value>Index the content of Downloads?</value></data>
  <data name="Set_DownloadsRisk" xml:space="preserve"><value>By default, Seekbeam does not read the content of your Downloads folder. Its files can still be found by name.

Why: files from the Internet and e-mail attachments land in Downloads. To index their content, Seekbeam would open and analyse each of them automatically, including files you never opened yourself. A document crafted to exploit a flaw in a file-format parser could then be processed without any action on your part.

Seekbeam reduces this risk: extraction runs in an isolated sandbox, without network access and without access to your other files. But no parser can be guaranteed free of flaws, and excluding Downloads removes this exposure entirely.

Index the content of Downloads anyway?</value></data>
